# Never wipe the database without asking

The Docker Postgres database (`onpoint_call`) is the real local dataset (imported leads, users, batches). Destroying it is a data-loss event. **Do not wipe it unless the user explicitly says to in this conversation.**

If a test, debug script, or “reset the environment” step would drop tables, **stop and ask first**. Do not proceed on implied consent, convenience, or a previous chat.

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly requested it

- `php artisan migrate:fresh` / `migrate:refresh` / `db:wipe` / `db:seed --class=...` after a wipe
- `Artisan::call('migrate:fresh')` (or refresh/wipe) in any script, tinker, or one-off PHP file
- `DROP DATABASE`, `DROP SCHEMA`, `TRUNCATE`, `DELETE FROM` without a narrow `WHERE`
- `docker compose down -v` (removes the `pgdata` volume)
- Setting `ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB=true` to bypass the app guard
- Pointing PHPUnit/`RefreshDatabase` at Postgres (`DB_CONNECTION=pgsql`, host `db`)

```php
// BAD — this wiped imported leads
Artisan::call('migrate:fresh', ['--force' => true]);

// GOOD — tests stay on sqlite :memory: (already enforced in tests/TestCase.php)
php artisan test
```

```bash
# BAD
docker compose exec app php artisan migrate:fresh --force
docker compose down -v

# GOOD — schema only, keeps data
docker compose exec app php artisan migrate --force
```

## Allowed without asking

- `php artisan migrate` (forward migrations only)
- `php artisan db:seed` **without** a preceding wipe, when adding missing reference data
- `php artisan test` using sqlite `:memory:` (never the Docker DB)
- Read-only `psql` / tinker selects

## If a wipe is truly required

1. Tell the user it will **permanently delete leads and other local data**.
2. Wait for an explicit yes in this chat (e.g. “wipe the database”).
3. Only then set `ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB=true` for that one command, then unset it.
